course: dictionary
lesson: 15052
title: Going backwards
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Retrograde is a long word, but it has two small parts. Retro means backwards, and grade means a step or a level. So retrograde means stepping backwards. «The team took a retrograde step when they lost their best player.» The clue is took a step: the team went back, not forward.
explain: Retrograde can describe a change that makes things worse. «Cutting the library's opening hours was a retrograde step for the village.» Nobody wants fewer books and less time to read, so the clues show this change is bad. Ask yourself: is the change going the right way, or the wrong way?
explain: In science, retrograde describes movement in the opposite direction to usual. «Mars seems to move backwards across the sky for a few weeks.» The clue is seems: Mars is not really going backwards. Earth passes it, so from our view it looks as if Mars is moving the other way.
fact: Retrograde means going backwards, or moving in the opposite direction to usual.
fact: «Retrograde motion» is when a planet seems to move backwards across the night sky for a while.
fact: Mars looks like it goes backwards because Earth overtakes it, like a faster car passing a slower one.
fact: «A retrograde step» means a change that makes things worse instead of better.
fact: In medicine, «retrograde amnesia» means losing memories from before an injury.
exercise: «The team took a retrograde step when they lost their best player.» What does retrograde mean here? | Running round the pitch twice | Playing in the rain | Scoring many goals | *Getting worse instead of better
exercise: «Retrograde motion» describes what? | A fish swimming towards the sea | *A planet that seems to move backwards across the sky | A bird that never stops flying | A car that drives in reverse for fun
exercise: Dad says, «Cutting the bus route was a retrograde step.» Is this good news or bad news? | Good news, because things got better | Good news, because buses are fast | Neither, because retrograde is a colour | *Bad news, because things got worse
test: «The doctor said Sam had retrograde amnesia, so he could not remember things from before his fall.» What does retrograde amnesia mean? | A sleepy feeling after a fall | Forgetting how to read | *Losing memories from before an injury | Remembering everything perfectly
test: The word retrograde is closest in meaning to which word? | Bright | *Backwards | Forward | Quick
exam: Which sentence uses retrograde to mean a change that makes things worse? | The sun rose in the retrograde | The class made a retrograde step by tidying the classroom | The rabbit had a retrograde tail | *Closing the pond at the park was a retrograde step for the wildlife
